  "content": {
    "id": "p12-q9-node",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "Solve the following equations and express your solutions to two decimal places where necessary.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p12-q9-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$4^x-6\\times 2^x+5=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=0$ or $x\\approx2.32$",
          "worked": "Let $u=2^x$, so $4^x=u^2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}u^2-6u+5&=0\\\\(u-1)(u-5)&=0\\end{align*}$$\nThus $u=1$ or $u=5$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2^x&=1\\\\x&=0\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}2^x&=5\\\\x&=\\frac{\\ln 5}{\\ln 2}\\\\x&\\approx2.32\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p12-q9-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$9^x-3^{x+1}+2=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=0$ or $x\\approx0.63$",
          "worked": "Let $u=3^x$. Then $9^x=u^2$ and $3^{x+1}=3u$.\n$$\\begin{align*}u^2-3u+2&=0\\\\(u-1)(u-2)&=0\\end{align*}$$\nThus $u=1$ or $u=2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}3^x&=1\\\\x&=0\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}3^x&=2\\\\x&=\\frac{\\ln 2}{\\ln 3}\\\\x&\\approx0.63\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 50
      },
      {
        "id": "p12-q9-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$25^x-5^{x+1}=6$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x\\approx1.11$.\n\nWith $u=5^x$, keep the root $u=6$ since $u$ must be positive.",
          "worked": "Let $u=5^x$. Then $25^x=u^2$ and $5^{x+1}=5u$.\n$$\\begin{align*}u^2-5u&=6\\\\u^2-5u-6&=0\\\\(u-6)(u+1)&=0\\end{align*}$$\nThe roots are $6$ and $-1$. Since $5^x>0$, use $u=6$.\n$$\\begin{align*}5^x&=6\\\\x&=\\frac{\\ln 6}{\\ln 5}\\\\x&\\approx1.11\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 50
      }
    ]
  },
